  "archive_id": "BW2-B43-P04",
  "title": "Nine B-Colors Suffice Through Ten Vertices for 3-Degenerate K3,4-Free Graphs of Maximum Degree at Most Four",
  "batch_label": "43",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For every finite simple graph G on at most ten vertices that is 3-degenerate (degeneracy at most 3), has maximum degree at most 4, and contains no K_{3,4} subgraph, q_B(G) is at most 9. This bound is sharp because q_B(K_{3,3})=9. Consequently, any legal graph with q_B(G)=10 must have a connected component on at least eleven vertices. This is an exact exhaustive computational result and does not determine M_3(4).",
